  "surprise": "Differential attention (Ye et al. 2024: two 16-dim softmax maps per head, softmax(q1 k1) - lambda softmax(q2 k2) on shared 32-dim values, lambda = exp(lq1.lk1) - exp(lq2.lk2) + lambda_init per block, headwise RMSNorm x (1 - lambda_init); 4,800,384 params as registered) on 115-fable scored 616/576/630 on seeds 0/1/2 vs the 639/646/609 of 115: exact means 607.33 vs 631.33, -24.0, paired -23/-70/+21, inside the registered -50..+50 range (central +10). Discard. The registered mechanism (a better-formed round-1 start from sharper premise retrieval at unseen lengths) is REFUTED in direction: round-1 targets solved 617/489/635 vs 718/756/691 (-101/-267/-56, every seed down), round-1 sample acc 0.244/0.166/0.259 vs 0.318/0.301/0.315, round-1 parse failures 14228/19956/8706 of 48,000 = 30/42/18% vs 25/22/18%; seed 1 repeated the milder form of the 104/112/116-fable seed-collapse pattern (42% unparseable, 489 solved). Expert iteration then climbed faster than on 115 (r1 to r4 +485/+527/+458 vs a mean +413) to 1102/1016/1093 RL-solved (mean 1070 vs 1131) but did not close the gap. Two surprises. (1) Cost: the second float-mask SDPA per block plus the head norm cost 32% of pretraining steps, 2827/2851/2845 vs 4204/4218/4263, well outside the predicted 3,300-3,900 (-8% to -22%), and RL sampling fell to 187-232 samples/s from 256-313, rounds took 277-346 s and totals were 1947/1878/1934 s vs 1572 (under the 2,400 s cap); like the canon layers of 109, a few extra small kernels per block are expensive in this launch-bound model. (2) Fit stayed close despite a third fewer steps: final val loss 0.0819/0.0850/0.0840 vs 0.0826/0.0806/0.0792 (minima 0.0789/0.0746/0.0796, all rising into the endpoint), held-out greedy 0.9835/0.983/0.9785 vs 0.9815/0.983/0.9845, so per step the differential heads fit the cap-6 data faster, yet that fit gave a worse 7+-line start, the pattern 112 (parallel block) showed. The mechanism was used, not ignored: learned lambda after pretraining 0.16/0.46/0.59/0.63/0.67/0.60 (s0), 0.15/0.35/0.59/0.75/0.65/0.57 (s1), 0.18/0.43/0.58/0.64/0.68/0.65 (s2) vs init 0.20/0.36/0.47/0.56/0.62/0.67, inside the predicted 0.1-0.9, with blocks 1-4 subtracting more than at init, and RL raised every block further (s0 final 0.16/0.50/0.61/0.66/0.72/0.64). Open hypotheses for the loss: 16-dim maps have too little resolution at this width to place a cited premise uniquely, so the subtraction cancels signal as well as noise; or the subtraction calibrated on cap-6 contexts over-suppresses at unseen lengths, as the steep decays of 113 and 117-fable did. A 32-dim-map version needs 16 maps per block (+786k params) and would cost even more steps. Lean gate: 119,583 parse failures of 800,736 samples vs 106,190 for 115; Lean vetoed 0 nd_verify-accepted proofs, 3 Lean-accepted proofs were rejected by nd_verify.",
